{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Every creeping thing that is alive, etc.</b> There is to know why flesh was not permitted to man but only to Noah. And it appears that from Noah's own merit they gave it to him for three reasons: First, that through his instrumentality HaShem found a way to sustain the species, and without him the species of creeping things would not have been sustained without man, and in this he earned a right over them. Second, that he toiled over them and labored in the ark — go out and learn how many labors he labored over them — and concerning him it is said (Psalms 128:2): ״יְגִיעַ כַּפֶּיךָ״ etc. Third, that through the instrumentality of his offering he caused HaShem's favor to be won, and He swore that He would never cut off all flesh, etc.; therefore HaShem permitted him to eat of the fruit of his way."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {0 "The citation תהילים קכ״ד:ב׳ appears to be a variant or abbreviation for Psalm 128:2 (תהילים קכח:ב), resolved from the Hebrew numerals as written."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:40:15.283486150Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}